# vulnprio secrets. Copy to .env and fill in what you have.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored and is never read into the config hash or the run manifest, so a key
# cannot leak into a report. A real environment variable always wins over this file, so an
# exported key or a CI secret is not shadowed by a stale file on disk.
#
# NONE of these are required. The default configuration runs the whole pipeline offline,
# with no key and no network, against fixtures and the synthetic world.

# Enables the model-backed assessment (llm.backend: anthropic) and the exploit-intelligence
# layer that searches the web for exploit material the feeds do not link.
# A live intelligence run costs roughly $0.13 per CVE.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. The exploit-intelligence layer's search half, when intel.search_provider is
# "parallel". Parallel is a pure search API with no model attached: it does the retrieving
# and whichever backend you configured does the interpreting, so this key pairs with one of
# the model keys rather than replacing it.
#
# In turbo mode a scan spends one search per finding at $1 per 1,000 searches -- $0.001 per
# finding, about a tenth of a cent, or ten cents for a hundred-finding scan. It exists
# because Google Search grounding has a far tighter quota than Gemini's generation does:
# grounded requests return 429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED on the free tier while plain generation
# succeeds seconds earlier, which leaves the free path with a working model and no working
# search. Keys are issued at https://platform.parallel.ai/
PARALLEL_API_KEY=

# Optional. Raises the NVD rate limit when feeds.mode is live or live_with_cache.
# Free from https://nvd.nist.gov/developers/request-an-api-key
NVD_API_KEY=
